{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Fifty and two hundred, etc., and you and Aaron, etc.</b> All of this is superfluous, for He already said <b>you and all your congregation</b>, etc., <b>and Aaron.</b> And if He wished to state their tally, above, when He said ״your congregation,״ there He should have said two hundred and fifty, and He would not have needed to go back and mention <b>you and Aaron.</b> Or perhaps He was wise not to let Korah intermingle with the two hundred and fifty, but rather separately, alone with Aaron; and He did so in order that there be no room for those who err after Korah to say that the evil cleaving to him was on account of his being together with the multitude of those offering incense — but had he been on his own, he would have been like Aaron. Therefore He said to him <b>and you and Aaron</b> — on your own, each man his fire-pan. And although they all offered together, with all this they became two parties — one party Korah and Aaron, and a second party two hundred and fifty men."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:12.986724942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}